 ## Overview
-Scale-Adaptive Gaussian Splatting (SA-GS) is a training-free, test-time plugin for 3D Gaussian Splatting that improves anti-aliasing by applying 2D scale-adaptive filters to each Gaussian primitive [S2, unofficial]. It solves the mismatch between Gaussian scales learned during training and the sampling frequency encountered at test time, which causes aliasing artifacts when zooming out or rendering at low resolutions [S2, unofficial]. Unlike [Mip-Splatting](6063-mip-splatting.md), which modifies the training procedure and uses filters unaware of testing frequency, SA-GS operates as a post-processing step informed by the specific rendering resolution and camera distance [S2, unofficial].
+Scale-Adaptive Gaussian Splatting (SA-GS) is a training-free, test-time plugin for 3D Gaussian Splatting that improves anti-aliasing by applying 2D scale-adaptive filters to each Gaussian primitive [S2, unofficial]. It solves the mismatch between Gaussian scales learned during training and the sampling frequency encountered at test time, which causes aliasing artifacts when zooming out or rendering at low resolutions [S2, unofficial]. Unlike [Mip-Splatting](6063-mip-splatting.md), which modifies the training procedure and uses 3D smoothing/2D Mip filters unaware of testing frequency, SA-GS operates at test-time and uses filters informed by testing frequency [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** Pre-trained 3D Gaussian field (positions, covariances, opacities, colors); camera parameters (view matrix, projection matrix, focal length); rendering resolution $(W, H)$.
-**Outputs:** Rendered image.
